{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>And this is the work of the lampstand.</b> The Holy One, blessed be He, showed it to him with His finger — for he found it difficult; therefore ״וְזֶה״ is said." "<b>Beaten work.</b> בטדי\"ץ בְּלַעַ\"ז — a term of ״דָּא לְדָא נָקְשָׁן״ (Daniel 5). It was a mass of a kikkar of gold, and he beats with a hammer and cuts with a chisel, to extend its limbs as required — and it was not made limb by limb by joining (see Sifra)." "<b>Unto its base.</b> Its יְרֵכָה is the shaft that is on the legs — hollow, like the manner of silver lampstands that stand before nobles." "<b>Unto its base, unto its flower.</b> That is, the body of the lampstand in its entirety and everything attached to it." "<b>Unto its base.</b> For it is a large limb." "<b>Until its base.</b> That is the finest work in it — all of it one piece; and the way ״עַד״ serves in this idiom is as in ״מִגָּדִישׁ וְעַד קָמָה וְעַד כֶּרֶם זַיִת״ (Judges 15)." "<b>As the appearance that He showed, etc.</b> Like the pattern that He showed him on the mountain, as it says (Exodus 25) — ״וּרְאֵה וַעֲשֵׂה בְּתַבְנִיתָם״ and so forth (Sifrei)." "<b>So he made the lampstand.</b> Who made it; and another interpretation: through the Holy One, blessed be He, it was made of itself (Tanchuma)."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {1 "The la'az בטדי\"ץ is Old French beteillier or similar; the exact Old French word is uncertain."}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:10:01.391775946Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}